{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced concat fusion with weighted fusion in the multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ResNet-50, avgpool setting (a single-variable change from llm_summary_007) to test whether learned fusion weights can downweight the weak image signal (image-only accuracy: 0.208) and address the underperformance observed with concat fusion. The validation accuracy of 0.678 (F1 0.646) exceeds the concat-fusion counterpart (0.632, F1 0.607) by ~4.6% and surpasses the RNA-only multiprofile baselines (0.650–0.653), indicating that weighted fusion allows the image modality to contribute positively on top of multiprofile RNA signal rather than degrading it; this is the highest validation accuracy observed in the study to date. It remains uncertain whether this gain is stable across repeated runs, whether alternative fusion or aggregation strategies could yield further improvements, and whether the weighted-fusion advantage is specific to the scVI_n200 encoder or generalizes across other encoder choices."
}

